\caption{Dataset and analysis design. (A) 4,645 cells from 19 melanoma samples (3CA study 3ca:20111) were analyzed using 1,360 metabolic genes from KEGG metabolic pathways. (B) Cell annotation counts: 4,097 annotated cells (4,049 epithelial, 48 immune, 100 stromal, 100 other), 548 unannotated cells. (C) UMAP embedding of cells colored by annotation, using 3CA-provided whole-transcriptome coordinates; metabolic gene re-fitting was not performed on this embedding. (D) Sample-level metadata: 19 patients, 4645 cells total, 1360 metabolic genes.}
\label{fig:dataset}
\end{figure}

\begin{figure}[!t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{../results/figures/figure2_metabolic_separation.pdf}
\caption{Metabolic gene separation. (A) PCA of 1,360 metabolic genes on 4,645 cells, with k-means clustering at k=2 yielding the highest silhouette score. (B) Silhouette scores across k=2..10 for all cells and k=2..8 for malignant cells, with k=2 identified as the optimum at the scan boundary. (C) Complexity residualization: silhouette scores after regressing out library complexity, confirming that metabolic state separation is not driven by sequencing depth. (D) Comparison against 20 random gene sets and a highly-variable-gene baseline; the metabolic gene set achieves the highest silhouette score, with the 95\% empirical range of random sets serving as a null reference (not a confidence interval). (E) Patient-blocked 5-fold cross-validation on 4,097 annotated cells using pooled row-normalized data, yielding balanced accuracy and macro-F1 for cell-type separation.}
\label{fig:separation}
\end{figure}

\begin{figure}[!t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{../results/figures/figure3_robustness_and_interpretation.pdf}
\caption{Robustness and interpretation. (A) Silhouette scores across k=2..6 for malignant cells (1,257 cells, 15 samples) after adjusting for patient and library complexity, with k=2 again identified as the boundary optimum. (B) PCA of malignant cells colored by patient, demonstrating patient-level clustering consistent with the k=2 metabolic state assignment. (C) Heatmap of mean expression across 18 KEGG metabolic pathways, standardized by cell type, showing distinct metabolic profiles between cell types without flux or scMetabolism scoring. (D) Alignment with sample and cell type using adjusted mutual information (AMI), confirming that metabolic gene states are not nested within training folds, patients, or cell types.}
\label{fig:robustness}
\end{figure}

